--- !u!114 &14178652330157687
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 9220374752839626139}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5f7201a12d95ffc409449d95f23cf332, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  m_Material: {fileID: 0}
  m_Color: {r: 0.19607843, g: 0.19607843, b: 0.19607843, a: 1}
  m_RaycastTarget: 1
  m_RaycastPadding: {x: 0, y: 0, z: 0, w: 0}
  m_Maskable: 1
  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_FontData:
    m_Font: {fileID: 10102, guid: 0000000000000000e000000000000000, type: 0}
    m_FontSize: 18
    m_FontStyle: 0
    m_BestFit: 0
    m_MinSize: 1
    m_MaxSize: 40
    m_Alignment: 0
    m_AlignByGeometry: 0
    m_RichText: 1
    m_HorizontalOverflow: 0
    m_VerticalOverflow: 0
    m_LineSpacing: 1
  m_Text: "GAMEPLAY:\n\n\tDuring gameplay walls will come towards the player. Your
    objective is to match your current shape with the incoming shape in the wall.
    Failure to match shape when passing through the wall, will cause the game to
    end. Hitting an area of the wall outside of the hole in the wall, will cause
    the game to end. You are able to go around the wall to collect coins if needed.
    \r\n\r\n\nCONTROLS: \n\n\tThere are different forms of movement in the game.
    Tapping the screen will cause the player to switch shapes, it also moves the
    player to the touch horizontal location. You can choose to slide left and right
    along the screen to move the player while the touch remains in contact. You are
    not able to move up or down. Releasing the touch releases control of the player.\r\n\r\n\nSHAPE
    CYCLE: \n\n\tThe shape exists along a cycle. The default shape you will start
    as is Circle. From there you will tap the screen. This will cause the shape to
    shift to Square. One more tap and you will arrive at the shape Triangle. HINT:
    Matching tap location to shape cycle is the key to your success. \r\n\r\n\nCOINS
    AND WALL COUNTER: \n\n\tThere are two factors to unlocking content in the game.
    The first option is to collect golden coins. The golden coins are a form of in
    game currency that can be used to purchase; Themes, Music, Shapes, Backgrounds.
    The wall counter is used to activate discounts for the items in the store. HINT:
    The more walls you successfully pass through, the further your money will go.
    \r\n\r\n\nSTORE: \n\n\tIn the store room you will see four categories. Music,
    Shapes, Background, Walls. You can purchase these items individually or purchase
    them as a theme package. These four categories can be interchanged. Items in
    the store will be removed, and added at different intervals so stay tuned. \r\n"
